# ============================================================
# NETLIFY REDIRECTS
# ============================================================
# Netlify serves this repo root exactly as it is committed, so
# every file in the repo is fetchable over HTTP unless a rule
# with a bang shadows it. These rules bounce the files that are
# not meant for the public back to the homepage.
#
# The band documents function holds every Drive link in one
# file. Without the first rule below, anyone could download
# that source at /netlify/functions/roadcase-links.mjs and read
# the lot without signing in. Do not remove it.
#
# The functions themselves are invoked at
# /.netlify/functions/<name>, with a leading dot, which none of
# these rules touch.
#
# Cutover note: DOMAIN-CUTOVER.md Step 4 adds a /home rule to
# this file when the domain moves. Add it above the blocks.
# ============================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# OLD SQUARESPACE URLS
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# The old site used extensionless URLs, this one uses .html.
# Netlify's extensionless fallback would already SERVE the right
# page at /about, but it answers 200, not 301. These rules make
# the move explicit so Google retires the old URL and hands the
# ranking to the .html page the canonicals point at.
#
# /home is the only one that genuinely 404s without a rule. The
# old homepage lived there, this one is at /.
#
# THE BANG ON THE FOUR .html RULES IS LOAD BEARING. Netlify only
# consults a redirect rule when nothing already answers the path,
# and its extensionless fallback resolves /about to about.html
# first, so an unforced rule never fires and the URL keeps
# answering 200. Verified live on 2026-08-15. /home needs no bang
# because nothing exists there.
#
# THIS LIST IS THE FIVE URLS VERIFIED IN DOMAIN-CUTOVER.md STEP 4.
# It is not proven to be every URL the old site had. Before the
# old site goes dark, pull the real inventory from Squarespace or
# from Search Console coverage and add anything missing here.
# ------------------------------------------------------------

/home                 /                  301
/about                /about.html        301!
/tour                 /tour.html         301!
/fan-photos           /fan-photos.html   301!
/band-gallery         /band-gallery.html 301!

# Function source, including every band document link.
/netlify/*            /    301!

# The Netlify config files themselves.
/_headers             /    301!
/_redirects           /    301!

# Internal runbook. Lists the GA4 property, the Formspree
# endpoint, and the repo. Not for the public.
/DOMAIN-CUTOVER.md    /    301!
